Defer deleting the Hyprland request socket until its readyRead slot returns;
deleting it inside the slot is a use-after-free.
Drop once Quickshell fixes https://github.com/quickshell-mirror/quickshell/issues/947

--- a/src/wayland/hyprland/ipc/connection.cpp
+++ b/src/wayland/hyprland/ipc/connection.cpp
@@ -190,5 +190,6 @@
-		auto responseCallback = [requestSocket, callback]() {
+		auto responseCallback = [this, requestSocket, callback]() {
 			auto response = requestSocket->readAll();
 			callback(true, std::move(response));
-			delete requestSocket;
+			QObject::disconnect(requestSocket, nullptr, this, nullptr);
+			requestSocket->deleteLater();
 		};
